---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import PillarGrid from '../components/PillarGrid.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="About"
	description="About Citizen Stewardship, a nonpartisan public project for American civic reform discussion."
>
	<PageHero
		title="About Citizen Stewardship"
		lede="Citizen Stewardship exists to publish serious democratic reform proposals for the United States in plain language so citizens can inspect, discuss, challenge, and improve them."
	/>

	<section class="section tight">
		<div class="container content-grid">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>What this project is</h2>
				<p>
					Citizen Stewardship is a citizen-created public project focused on democratic
					renewal in the United States. It is built around the idea that democratic
					institutions should be protected from corruption, concentrated private power,
					misinformation, and permanent political careerism.
				</p>
				<p>
					The project is intentionally nonpartisan. It does not ask readers to support a
					party. It asks readers to examine rules, safeguards, incentives, and civic duties
					that could help the U.S. government answer to the public.
				</p>
				<p>
					The proposals are drafts for discussion and refinement. They should be tested against
					history, constitutional law, political feasibility, administrative complexity, civil
					liberties, and unintended consequences.
				</p>

				<h2>What this project is not</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>It is not legal advice.</li>
					<li>It is not an official government document.</li>
					<li>It is not a party platform or campaign committee.</li>
					<li>It is not a data-collection site.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<aside class="callout">
				<h3>Operating standard</h3>
				<p>
					Good civic reform should be public, readable, accountable, legally honest, and open to
					hard criticism.
				</p>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section surface-band">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-header">
				<h2>What Citizen Stewardship Stands For</h2>
				<p>
					The core pillars are the values used to judge whether a reform belongs in this
					project. A proposal should generally strengthen public accountability, ordinary
					citizen power, equality, transparency, education, and limits on corporate capture.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="content-grid">
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						Citizen Stewardship is not trying to hand public power from one party to
						another. It is meant to ask whether public systems can be made harder to buy,
						harder to hide, harder to abuse, and easier for people to understand and repair.
					</p>
					<p>
						Disagreement is welcome. Suggestions should still be compatible with equal
						rights, nonpartisanship, public accountability, and democratic repair. A useful
						reform can challenge an existing proposal, but it should do so in a way that
						builds a more durable and fair public system.
					</p>
				</div>
				<PillarGrid compact />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
